@page "/coding-agent"

@* The coding agent at work (F120): a session recorded once, played back in the framework's chat view, then the offer.
   One slide, side by side (FX105): the words on the left, read while the session plays in the window on the right. The
   live chat stays closed to visitors (FX88), so this is the door the header and the hero lead to. *@

<PageTitle>The coding agent · louis-agent</PageTitle>
<PageDescription Text="Watch the louis-agent coding agent fix a real bug: it runs the tests, reads the code, fixes it on a branch and runs the tests again." />

<Band Id="top" Kicker="The coding agent">
    <div class="watch-grid">
        <div class="watch-text">
            <h2 class="chrome">Watch it fix a real bug.</h2>
            <p class="lede">A small invoice matcher, and bank payments that don't find their invoices. This is the session as it happened, played back. Nothing runs while you watch.</p>
            <ul class="rules">
                <li><strong>Every tool is a pack.</strong> It reads the files, runs the tests and writes the fix with the files, git and dotnet packs, the same ones it uses in Rider and the terminal.</li>
                <li><strong>It checks its own work.</strong> Two tests fail before the fix and all four pass after it, and it says which and why.</li>
                <li><strong>It leaves the commit to you.</strong> The fix sits in the working tree, and it says so.</li>
                <li><strong>It cost about R0.10.</strong> Seven requests on Claude Haiku, priced by the usage ledger, the bill under the answer.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="band-note">The live agent runs shell commands, so here it runs only for its owner, behind a key.</p>
        </div>
        <RecordedChat Source="recordings/coding-session.sse" Question="@Question" Title="the coding agent · toolsets: files, git, dotnet" PlayAgain="Play it again" Currency="Rand">
            <Ending>
                <p class="recorded-offer">Want an agent like this on your own code? <a href="/contact">Ask for yours</a>.</p>
                <GuideButton Question="I watched the coding agent fix the invoice matcher. Could I get an agent like that for my team?">Ask the guide about one</GuideButton>
            </Ending>
        </RecordedChat>
    </div>
</Band>
